{"name":"Cavern Sand","hex":"#947054","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cavern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large cave.","An underground chamber."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To form a cavern or deep depression in.","To put into a cavern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cavern"},{"term":"sand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock that is ground more finely than gravel, but is not as fine as silt (more formally, see grain sizes chart), forming beaches and deserts and also used in construction.\n\n A specific grade, type, or composition of sand.\n\n A beach or other mass of sand.","A specific grade, type, or composition of sand."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light beige colour, like that of typical sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cave","blocks":[{"text":"Caves and caverns are natural voids under the surface of the Earth and have also been observed in other rocky worlds. Caves often form by the weathering of rock and can extend deep underground. Exogene caves are smaller openings that extend a relatively short distance underground. Caves which extend farther underground than the opening is wide are called endogene caves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Lechuguilla_Cave_Pearlsian_Gulf.jpg/330px-Lechuguilla_Cave_Pearlsian_Gulf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/HallOfTheMountainKings.jpg/500px-HallOfTheMountainKings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/HallOfTheMountainKings.jpg/500px-HallOfTheMountainKings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Speleothems in Hall of the Mountain King of Ogof Craig a Ffynnon, a solutional cave in South Wales.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHallOfTheMountainKings.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Hawaiian_lava_tube.jpg/500px-Hawaiian_lava_tube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Hawaiian_lava_tube.jpg/500px-Hawaiian_lava_tube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Exploring a lava tube in Hawaii.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHawaiian_lava_tube.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Painted_cave.jpg/500px-Painted_cave.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa